===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|mechanics}} An opening into which a [[plug]] or other connecting part is designed to fit (e.g. ''a [[light bulb]] socket'').
#: {{syn|en|jack}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2021 December 29|title=Network News: HS2 rolling stock|journal=RAIL|issue=947|page=7|text=Each seat must have a 230V '''socket''', a USB '''socket''', a coat hook, reading light and cup holder.}}
# {{lb|en|anatomy}} A [[hollow]] into a [[bone]] which a part fits, such as an [[eye]], or another bone, in the case of a [[joint]].
# {{lb|en|computing}} One endpoint of a [[two-way]] communication link, used for [[interprocess communication]] across a network.
# {{lb|en|computing}} One endpoint of a [[two-way]] [[named pipe]] on Unix and Unix-like systems, used for [[interprocess communication]].
# A hollow tool for grasping and lifting tools dropped in a well-boring.
# The hollow of a [[candlestick]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1671|author=[[w:Thomas Watson (Puritan)|Thomas Watson]]|title=The Beatitudes|page=8
|passage=Chriſt calls his Miniſters, ''Lux Mundi'', ''the light of the World'', Matth. 5. 14. therefore they must be alwayes giving forth their luſtre; their light must not go out till it be in the '''ſocket''' or till violent death as an extinguisher put it out.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|title=Erlesmere; or, Contrasts of Character|year=1856|passage=The candle burned to its '''socket''', the fire went out, the night air grew heavy with silence, before Herbert lay down.|author=L. S. Lavenu|page=336|pageurl=https://www.google.ca/books/edition/Erlesmere_or_Contrasts_of_character/tTQv8p7ynJgC?hl=en&gbpv=1&pg=PA336|chapter=XXXIII|volume=1|publisher=Smith, Elder & Co.|location=London|url=https://www.google.ca/books/edition/Erlesmere_or_Contrasts_of_character/tTQv8p7ynJgC?hl=en&gbpv=0}}
# A steel apparatus attached to a [[saddle]] to protect the thighs and legs.

